==English==
[[Image:Valeriana officinalis jfg1.jpg|thumb|A '''valerian''' plant in bloom.]]
{{wikipedia|valerian (plant)}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro}} {{term|valeriane}} or mediaeval {{etyl|la}} {{term|valeriana}}, from the personal name {{term|Valerius}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/vəˈlɪəɹɪən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hardy]] [[perennial]] [[flowering plant]], ''[[Valeriana officinalis]]'', with heads of [[sweet]]ly [[scent]]ed pink or white [[flower]]s.
# More generally, any plant of the genus [[Valeriana]].
# {{uncountable}} The root of ''Valeriana officinalis'', used in herbal medicine.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|Valeriana officinalis}} [[allheal]], [[cat thyme]]

